# Every file checked out as committed, whatever the machine's core.autocrlf says (Git for Windows'
# system config sets it true: a fresh clone on another PC got CRLF in the build.kpp copies and
# kpp-native's headers, and convert.cmd's line-end check failed, 2026-11-05). Each file keeps the
# line ends it has in the repository (CLAUDE.md: resolver.cpp LF, codegen.cpp CRLF); the rules
# below, which come later, win over this one.
* -text

# cmd.exe finds labels (goto, call :label) unreliably in a batch file of LF line ends: CRLF in
# the working tree, LF in the repository.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# A snippet about a CRLF file (a raw string literal across its line ends) keeps its CRs as committed.
compiler/tests/spec/language/raw_string_in_crlf_file.kpp -text
